questions.question:
The treasurer of a regional bank is updating next year’s term structures. Four items are under discussion:

(i) the rollover of term deposits maturing in March, as planned in the budget;

(ii) a senior bond issue in June to fund the planned growth of the mortgage book;

(iii) the sale of unencumbered government bonds to cover a negative cumulated position in September;

(iv) a drawdown of a committed credit line received from another bank, kept for emergencies. Which items belong in the term structure of expected cash flows (TSECF)?
